# ORIGINAL hand-authored 2CV-inspired study. No logos or downloaded geometry.
# SOURCE: edit this file and car_2cv.mtl; generate-2cv-model.py never rewrites them.
# +Y up, +Z front; approximate metres. Four 12-sided tires touch Y=0.
# Flat normals: normalize(cross(b-a,c-a)); DCM1 intentionally stores no normals.
# Closed overlapping body/cabin/bonnet, wheels, lamps and bumpers; NOT a welded union.
# Glass, canvas, hubcaps, wings, grille and tail lamps are outward-facing open patches.
# Local negative position indices keep each named part independently editable.
# Atlas UVs: blue, cream, glass, rubber / metal, canvas, headlamp, taillamp.
# Paired side panels use mirrored diagonals, including nonplanar shoulders.
# Central planar quads may retain different diagonals, but identical surfaces.
mtllib car_2cv.mtl
s off
vt 0.125 0.750
vt 0.375 0.750
vt 0.625 0.750
vt 0.875 0.750
vt 0.125 0.250
vt 0.375 0.250
vt 0.625 0.250
vt 0.875 0.250

